{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101995","id":2297431368,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc6I8AVI","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101995","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101995.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101995.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101995","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101995/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/101995/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101995/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/e091396f6ea8f5e6f414ed42e72541084d6b4dfb","number":101995,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Core: Decouple `Variant` enums to standalone file","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This PR creates a separate file for Variant's enums, similar to what Input has done. However, unlike the Input enums, this keeps them as regular enums but within a namespaced scope:\r\n```cpp\r\nnamespace godot {\r\nnamespace details {\r\n\r\nenum VariantType { ... }\r\nenum VariantOperator { ... }\r\n\r\n} // namespace details\r\n} // namespace godot\r\n\r\nusing VariantType = godot::details::VariantType;\r\nusing VariantOperator = godot::details::VariantOperator;\r\n```\r\nThese \"namespaced\" enums are a sort of middle-ground between legacy & scoped enums, where the type can be hoisted to the global namespace *without* also adding the enum constants with it. That is, the enum values will require a preceeding type, but are otherwise identical to legacy enums. Fully backwards-compatible bindings have been setup in `Variant`, ensuring this PR does not break compatibility out of the gate.\r\n\r\nThe purpose of this is to allow for typing logic & conditionals to be applied **without** requiring a `variant.h` include. Currently, that include severly impairs type binding tools, as they cannot properly create advanced type logic until it's too late. Similarly, this would allow for explicitly binding these enums are argument/return types for scopes prior to Variant being defined, as you cannot forward declare a nested enum. Arrays and dictionaries are by far the biggest winners from this change, as they'd be able to use `VariantType` immediately & `TypedArray`/`TypedDictionary` could have their name/bind logic consolidated to the regular headers of each respective type (what #96741 tried to accomplish).\r\n\r\nI believe that the decoupling warrants the PR in and of itself, with explicit integration happening in subsequent PRs, but I'm open to expanding this scope instead if desired.","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":279096997,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwy